 of these medications can have implications for nutritional management in patients undergoing such treatments.\",2\r\n2834,FIBRINÓGENO,\"Fibrinogen is a crucial blood plasma protein that plays a vital role in blood clot formation and wound healing. It is essential for the coagulation process, helping to prevent excessive bleeding when injuries occur. Additionally, fibrinogen levels are closely monitored in patients undergoing anticoagulation therapy and those with thrombotic conditions, as these levels can indicate the body's ability to form clots effectively. Overall, fibrinogen is integral to maintaining hemostasis and is a key factor in the management of various blood-related health issues.\",2\r\n11099,LINFOCITOS T,\"LINFOCITOS T, or T lymphocytes, are a type of white blood cell that play a central role in cell-mediated immunity. They are crucial for the immune response, helping the body to identify and eliminate pathogens and infected cells.\",2\r\n11103,TRATAMIENTO CONSERVADOR,\"\"\"TRATAMIENTO CONSERVADOR\"\" refers to a management approach that employs non-surgical methods to address medical conditions such as chylothorax and chylous ascites. This treatment strategy emphasizes dietary modifications and medical therapies as initial interventions, prioritizing resolution of the condition without resorting to invasive surgical options.\",2\r\n11161,EMBOLIZACIÓN,\"Embolization is a minimally invasive procedure used to treat conditions such as quilotórax and lymphatic fistulas, showing high success rates in traumatic cases.\",1\r\n11100,LINFOCITOS B,B lymphocytes are a type of white blood cell that produce antibodies and are essential for humoral immunity.,1\r\n11097,LINFOGRAFÍA,La linfografía es una técnica de imagen utilizada para evaluar el sistema linfático y puede ser útil en el diagnóstico de quilotórax.,1\r\n11093,TORACOCENTESIS,\"La toracocentesis es un procedimiento médico utilizado para extraer líquido del espacio pleural, que puede ayudar en el diagnóstico del quilotórax.\",1\r\n11096,TÉCNICAS DE IMAGEN,Las técnicas de imagen son métodos utilizados para diagnosticar y localizar lesiones en condiciones como el quilotórax.,1\r\n11101,QUILOTÓRAX ASOCIADO A TUMOR,\"Quilotórax associated with a tumor refers to the condition of lymphatic fluid accumulation in the pleural cavity that is linked to the presence of a tumor, affecting prognosis.\",1\r\n4388,TOMOGRAFÍA AXIAL COMPUTARIZADA,\"Tomografía Axial Computarizada, also known as CT scan, is a diagnostic imaging technique utilized to create detailed images of internal organs, which is frequently employed in medical evaluations. This advanced imaging method allows for the identification of the location and causes of various medical conditions, including specific issues such as chylothorax.\",1\r\n10173,TIPS,\"TIPS, or Transjugular Intrahepatic Portosystemic Shunt, is a medical procedure designed to address portal hypertension, which is frequently associated with liver disease. This procedure is particularly beneficial for treating conditions such as quilotórax that arise as a secondary complication of portal hypertension. By creating a shunt, TIPS offers a potential resolution for these conditions, improving patient outcomes related to elevated portal pressure.\",1\r\n13783,ALOANTÍGENOS,\"Los aloantígenos son antígenos que son diferentes entre individuos de la misma especie, y pueden provocar una respuesta inmune en el receptor de un injerto.\",1\r\n\n\n-----Relationships-----\nhuman_readable_id,source,target,description,combined_degree\r\n3221,PACIENTE,EQUIPO MÉDICO,El equipo médico supervisa y trata al paciente durante su recuperación y evolución clínica,550\r\n3205,PACIENTE,DRENAJE,La paciente tuvo un drenaje postoperatorio para manejar complicaciones tras la cirugía bariátrica,549\r\n4759,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,QUILOTÓRAX,\"NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL is utilized in cases of QUILOTÓRAX, particularly when enteral nutrition is insufficient or not feasible. This form of nutriti